The Nightblade is the evil elite of the Assassin (rogue route, alignment -30
at promotion). It marks one victim at a time, finishes the wounded, and
poisons the rest.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks</ansi>

  30 Death Mark        its first target each battle is marked, left
                       exposed for 2 rounds (an opening for Opening
                       Strike), and takes 60% more damage from it;
                       when that foe falls, the mark passes to the
                       most hurt foe in reach, exposed again
  35 Envenom           its blows poison the target a third of the
                       time
  40 Keener finish     Finisher works on a foe at or below 60% health
  45 Shadowstep        once every 3 rounds it may strike the marked foe
                       in the middle row as if it had extended reach;
                       guardians can still intercept
  50 Hunting the mark  +25% critical chance against the marked foe
  55 Killing Spree     when it fells the marked foe, its action meter
                       gains 50, once a round
  60 Coup de Grace     a blow that lands on a foe below 20% health
                       fells it outright; against a boss it deals
                       double damage instead

Meter points speed up a turn; they never grant an extra one. The mark, the
poison and the spree last only for the battle and are never saved.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Elite talents</ansi>

Rogue elite talents (levels 35, 45, 55): Shadow Footing (+5 Evasion), Razor's
Edge (+5% critical chance), Quick Hands (+15 opening action meter). Every
elite rogue may take them. See <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.


See also: <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help rogue-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help abilities</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help statuses</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.
